    {
      "file": "libr/bin/p/bin_omf.c",
      "function": "check_buffer",
      "line": null,
      "code": "ut16 rec_size = ut8p_bw (buf + 1);",
      "note": "`check_buffer` dereferences the OMF header's two-byte size field from `buf + 1` without first rejecting buffers shorter than the 4-byte header. The later size predicate is below this dereference, so it cannot protect truncated inputs. The patch fixes this exact obligation by switching to bounded `r_buf_read_le16_at()` / `r_buf_read_at()` helpers and querying the buffer size explicitly.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
